WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.590
And it's time for Drew's News,

2
00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:03.710
your friendly news gardeners

3
00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:06.340
planting those good news seeds.

4
00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:07.690
And with me at the desk,

5
00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:09.590
best co-pilot on the planet,

6
00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:11.770
and I do mean that, Rossy Ross Mathews.

7
00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:13.990
Hi, hi, everybody!
(audience clapping)

8
00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:15.050
Spring, sprung!

9
00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:17.310
Today, I'm really excited,

10
00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:19.430
because we have an epic desk guest.

11
00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:22.310
She is a writer, an actress, an entrepreneur,

12
00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:24.620
and you can catch her on the seventh and final season

13
00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:25.700
of "Grace and Frankie."

14
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.206
Please welcome our dear friend to the show,

15
00:00:28.206 --> 00:00:29.864
June Diane Raphael!

16
00:00:29.864 --> 00:00:33.110
Oh my god, it's good to be here.

17
00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:34.070
It feels right.

18
00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:35.973
It feels really right.

19
00:00:35.973 --> 00:00:40.910
I mean, you and your often collaborator,

20
00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:42.320
Casey Wilson,

21
00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:44.070
were kind enough to come on the show

22
00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:46.300
when nobody knew what it was.

23
00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.270
We were in the height of a pandemic.

24
00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:51.300
And thank you for taking that leap with us back in the day.

25
00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.713
Are you kidding me?
(audience clapping)

26
00:00:53.713 --> 00:00:55.580
What?
And then, fun fact.

27
00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:58.310
What?
Your husband, Paul,

28
00:00:58.310 --> 00:01:00.100
is the first person

29
00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:03.920
who brought the Drew's News Zoom to life.

30
00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:04.830
Oh yeah, the background.

31
00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:06.640
And we've followed his model ever since.

32
00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:08.330
But he's the origin story.

33
00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:10.059
That's her husband, Paul Scheer.

34
00:01:10.059 --> 00:01:11.122
(audience clapping)

35
00:01:11.122 --> 00:01:13.980
Should I be expecting like some commission on this show?

36
00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:15.743
There might be a residual check in the mail.

37
00:01:15.743 --> 00:01:18.090
Do I get a cut?
Yeah, you do.

38
00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:19.180
I should.

39
00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:23.310
Speaking of cuts, that dress, you are looking so beautiful

40
00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:26.270
and you work alongside of two legends,

41
00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:28.440
Lily Tomlin and Jane Fonda.

42
00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:32.167
This is the final season of "Grace and Frankie."

43
00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:36.060
The show has lasted seven seasons.

44
00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:37.420
It's crazy.

45
00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:38.955
Seven!
And it's so good.

46
00:01:38.955 --> 00:01:40.622
I love it so much.

47
00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:44.170
And listen, so it's interesting

48
00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.210 line:15%
to kind of talk about it now 'cause it's coming out,

49
00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:48.400 line:15%
the final season premieres April 29th,

50
00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:50.610 line:15%
but we finished in November.

51
00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:53.880
Any fun, fly on the wall, surprises

52
00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:56.110
about the icons of Jane and Lily

53
00:01:56.110 --> 00:01:57.960
that come off the top of your head.

54
00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:00.763
I mean, I think they were very nervous to work with me.

55
00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:02.820
You know what I mean?

56
00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:05.750
Just to be in the presence of a legend.

57
00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:06.583
That's right.

58
00:02:06.583 --> 00:02:07.416
You're damn straight.
And icon.

59
00:02:07.416 --> 00:02:08.680
So I just tried to tell them

60
00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:11.410
like I'm just a regular gal, you know?

61
00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:13.950
Like there's nothing to be worried about.

62
00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:15.123
So sweet of you.

63
00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:17.990
I think the thing I love

64
00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:21.250
the most about them is how often

65
00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:25.554
both Jane and Lily use Siri.

66
00:02:25.554 --> 00:02:27.110
Whoa, really?
Yeah.

67
00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:28.222
I love this!

68
00:02:28.222 --> 00:02:29.055
That's so fun!

69
00:02:29.055 --> 00:02:33.350
It's just, I mean, I'm using Siri very occasionally.

70
00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:35.690
You know, very judiciously.

71
00:02:35.690 --> 00:02:40.140
But they are fully transcribing texts to people

72
00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:43.023
and full emails, new paragraph.

73
00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:47.830
They're fully living their lives on Siri.

74
00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:50.510
Ah, this is the best tip ever, I love it.

75
00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:52.210
I love this intel.
It's so interesting.

76
00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:54.310
I feel like Siri doesn't like me.

77
00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:56.630
But if it's good enough for Jane and Lily,

78
00:02:56.630 --> 00:02:58.179
it is good enough for everyone, but me.

79
00:02:58.179 --> 00:03:00.762 line:15%
(upbeat music)

